<%# locals: (label:, items:, per_view: 3, id: nil, slide_label: nil, data: {}, class_name: nil, style: :standard, caption: nil, start: nil, autoplay: nil, loop: false) %>
<%# THE CAROUSEL: one sideways row of slides, the apps' standard for a set too
    long to grid. Render it as a layout, so each slide is your own block:

      render layout: "studio/carousel", locals: { label: "Portfolio", items: @apps } do |app|
        render "apps/card", app: app
      end

      label        the region's accessible name. Required: a screen reader says
                   "Portfolio, carousel".
      items        one slide per item; the block draws it.
      per_view     whole slides in view on a wide row (1 to 6). A medium row shows
                   up to two, a phone one, and every width shows a sliver of the
                   next slide, so a visitor sees there is more.
      id           the track's id, for the arrows' aria-controls. Defaults from
                   the label; pass one when two carousels on a page share a label.
      slide_label  a callable that names a slide from its item. Without one a
                   slide is "2 of 6".
      data         data attributes for the region, such as a test hook.
      class_name   classes for the region, such as its width.
      style        :standard (slides snap to the start) or :spotlight (the
                   centred slide is full size and colour, its neighbours smaller,
                   faded and grey, and the arrows and keys move one slide).
      caption      a callable that writes a line under a slide from its item. A
                   standard row shows a small line under every slide; the
                   spotlight shows it under the centred slide only.
      start        the slide the row opens on: an index from 0, or :middle (the
                   slide at items.size / 2). Defaults to :middle for a spotlight
                   that does not loop, so both halves of the row hold a slide at
                   load, and to 0 for a standard row and for a looping spotlight
                   (its wrap already shows the last slide left of the first, so it
                   opens on the host's first item). An explicit start: wins. The browser sets it before the first paint where
                   it has scroll-initial-target; elsewhere the controller sets it
                   when it connects, with no glide and nothing announced. A link
                   to an id inside the row (#fragment) wins over the start.
      loop         true wraps the row, and a row of more than one slide is
                   visually continuous: the controller copies the last slides
                   before the first and the first after the last, so the first
                   slide centred shows the last beside it. Next at the last slide
                   glides on to the first, Previous at the first back to the last,
                   then the row jumps silently onto the real slide (no glide under
                   reduced motion), and neither arrow is ever disabled. A copy is
                   aria-hidden and inert, with no id, name, test hook or controller,
                   so a screen reader and Tab meet each slide once, a #fragment
                   finds the real slide, and the dots and "slide N of M" count the
                   real slides. Every slide of a looping row is a stop.
      autoplay     seconds between moves (a number above 0); nil, the default, is
                   off. The row moves one slide each interval and holds still while
                   the pointer is over the slides, while keyboard focus is in it,
                   while the tab is hidden or the row is off screen, and after a
                   swipe or press until the reader leaves it alone a while. A pause
                   button sits beside the arrows (WCAG 2.2.2). Under reduced motion
                   the row starts stopped, and Play starts it. Without loop it
                   stops at the last slide; Play then starts again from the first.

    THE SPOTLIGHT (engine.css, carousel-spotlight) snaps each slide to the centre.
    Where the browser has scroll-driven animations, each slide's own view timeline
    scales and fades it as it nears the centre, so the effect follows the finger.
    Elsewhere the controller marks the centred slide (data-current) and CSS
    transitions it. Under reduced motion nothing scales: the neighbours are only
    dimmed.

    THE TRACK IS A NATIVE SCROLL-SNAP ROW (engine.css, carousel). A swipe, a
    trackpad, a wheel and a focused link move it with no script. The carousel
    controller (studio/controllers/carousel_controller) adds the edge fade, the
    arrows, the dots and the keys, and until it connects the controls stay
    hidden and the row keeps a thin scrollbar. The widths come from container
    queries on the region, so a carousel in a narrow column lays out as a phone
    does.

    ACCESSIBLE BY THE APG CAROUSEL PATTERN: a labelled region with
    aria-roledescription carousel, a focusable track named "<label> slides", each
    slide a group with aria-roledescription slide and its own label, named arrows
    that set aria-disabled at an end (not disabled, so focus stays on the arrow),
    and a polite, atomic status line that speaks only after a press that moves the
    row (a looping row's arrows are never disabled; autoplay never speaks). A key pressed in a form field, an arrow-key widget (a slider, a tab list,
    a listbox...) or a nested carousel stays that element's. %>
<%
  per_view = per_view.to_f.clamp(1, 6)
  per_view = per_view.to_i if per_view == per_view.floor
  items = items.to_a
  total = items.size
  spotlight = case style.to_s
              when "standard" then false
              when "spotlight" then true
              else raise ArgumentError, "studio/carousel style: #{style.inspect} is not :standard or :spotlight"
              end
  loop = loop ? true : false
  wraps = loop && total > 1
  # A looping spotlight has a left neighbour at its first slide (the clones), so it
  # opens there; one that does not loop opens mid-row so neither half is empty.
  start = spotlight && !wraps ? :middle : 0 if start.nil?
  start_index = case start
                when :middle, "middle" then total / 2
                when Integer then start.clamp(0, [total - 1, 0].max)
                else raise ArgumentError, "studio/carousel start: #{start.inspect} is not an index or :middle"
                end
  autoplay = nil if autoplay == false
  unless autoplay.nil? || (autoplay.is_a?(Numeric) && autoplay.positive? && autoplay.finite?)
    raise ArgumentError, "studio/carousel autoplay: #{autoplay.inspect} is not a number of seconds above 0 or nil"
  end
  autoplay = autoplay.to_i if autoplay && autoplay == autoplay.floor
  arrow_noun = spotlight ? "slide" : "slides"
  track_id = id.presence || "carousel-#{label.to_s.parameterize.presence || 'slides'}"
%>
<%= tag.section(class: ["carousel", ("carousel-spotlight" if spotlight), class_name].compact.join(" "),
      role: "region",
      aria: { roledescription: "carousel", label: label },
      style: "--carousel-per-view: #{per_view}",
      data: { studio_controller: "carousel", studio_action: "keydown->carousel#key", carousel_start: (start_index.to_s if start_index.positive?),
              carousel_autoplay: (autoplay.to_s if autoplay), carousel_loop: ("" if loop) }.compact.merge(data)) do %>
  <%# The track takes focus for the keys, so it carries a name: a group, since a
      bare div may not be named. %>
  <div id="<%= track_id %>" class="carousel-track" tabindex="0" role="group"
       aria-label="<%= label %> slides" data-carousel-target="track">
    <% items.each_with_index do |item, index| %>
      <div class="carousel-slide" role="group" aria-roledescription="slide"
           aria-label="<%= slide_label ? slide_label.call(item) : "#{index + 1} of #{total}" %>"
           data-carousel-target="slide"<%= ' data-carousel-start-slide'.html_safe if start_index.positive? && index == start_index %><%= ' data-current'.html_safe if spotlight && index == start_index %>><% if spotlight %><div class="carousel-spotlight-body"><%= yield(item) %></div><% else %><%= yield(item) %><% end %><% if caption %><div class="carousel-caption"><%= caption.call(item) %></div><% end %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="carousel-controls">
    <div class="carousel-dots" role="group" aria-label="Choose a slide">
      <% total.times do |index| %>
        <button type="button" class="carousel-dot" aria-label="Go to slide <%= index + 1 %>"
                aria-controls="<%= track_id %>"<%= ' aria-current="true"'.html_safe if index == start_index %>
                data-carousel-target="dot" data-carousel-index="<%= index %>"
                data-studio-action="click->carousel#goTo"></button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="carousel-arrows">
      <% if autoplay %>
        <%# The pause button (WCAG 2.2.2). The controller renames it "Play slideshow"
            and swaps the icon when the reader stops the row. %>
        <button type="button" class="carousel-button carousel-autoplay" aria-label="Pause slideshow" aria-controls="<%= track_id %>"
                data-carousel-target="toggle" data-studio-action="click->carousel#toggle">
          <svg class="carousel-autoplay-pause" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5.5" y="4.5" width="3" height="11" rx="1"/><rect x="11.5" y="4.5" width="3" height="11" rx="1"/></svg>
          <svg class="carousel-autoplay-play" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 4.8v10.4a.8.8 0 0 0 1.2.7l8.2-5.2a.8.8 0 0 0 0-1.4L8.2 4.1A.8.8 0 0 0 7 4.8Z"/></svg>
        </button>
      <% end %>
      <button type="button" class="carousel-button" aria-label="Previous <%= arrow_noun %>" aria-controls="<%= track_id %>"
              aria-disabled="<%= !wraps && start_index.zero? %>" data-carousel-target="prev" data-studio-action="click->carousel#prev">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12.5 15 7.5 10l5-5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="carousel-button" aria-label="Next <%= arrow_noun %>" aria-controls="<%= track_id %>"
              <%= 'aria-disabled="true" '.html_safe if !wraps && total.positive? && start_index == total - 1 %>data-carousel-target="next" data-studio-action="click->carousel#next">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.5 5 5 5-5 5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-carousel-target="status"></p>
<% end %>
